<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Perfect! Let’s go!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Arthur</span> grabs you by the hand and the two of you begin to scour the playground for anything useful. <br>
<br>
<span style="color:Yellow">It is only 30 minutes later when panic starts to set in for the boy. Together, you’ve only managed to find a single discarded sock, a suspiciously moist child’s zip-up hoodie, and a 5 dollar bill submerged in a puddle too muddy to be worth grabbing. Overall, a bust and <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Arthur</span> seems to begin to panic.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Ahhhh! Why does today have to be the day the park is actually clean!? I find buttons here all the time! Then the one time I NEED buttons I can’t find a single one!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Arthur</span> slumps back down on the swing looking defeated. <br>
<br>
You walk up behind him and pat him on the back reassuringly. Finding exactly what he needed at this playground was a longshot to begin with, so you should probably just head to the thrift store and try to buy what he needs. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yeah…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Arthur</span> looks up with a nervous smile, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“About that… I already spent all my allowance on the prototype, and the original, and the pieces I could get for the second original… So… I’m broke.”</span> You sigh, facepalming, and offer to spot the boy a couple bucks, but he quickly refuses. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“No way! This hat has to be special! I can’t just take money off you, I have to earn it! Through blood, sweat, and tears if I must!”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:Pink">You admire his enthusiasm, but he can’t really make buttons out of blood, sweat, and tears.</span> <br>
<br>

